        "section_id": "MA-S2",
        "writer_text": "## Motivation: limitations of vanilla SSMs – they ignore irregular timespans and are vulnerable to input noise\n\nStandard state-space models assume uniform timesteps and therefore ignore the irregular timespans that characterize real-world interaction sequences, and their state update provides no explicit mechanism to suppress unreliable or noisy transitions. These two limitations motivate the timespan-aware and noise-robust design choices that follow.",
